.TH tensor-wasm-observe 1  "tensor-wasm-observe "
.SH NAME
tensor\-wasm\-observe \- Live operator dashboard over /healthz + /metrics (refreshes in place)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtensor\-wasm observe\fR [\fB\-\-addr\fR=\fIADDR\fR] [\fB\-\-interval\fR=\fIINTERVAL\fR] [\fB\-\-tenant\fR=\fITENANT\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Polls \fBGET /healthz\fR and \fBGET /metrics\fR against the target server on a fixed cadence and rewrites a single screen with the most actionable signals. Intended for on\-call incident triage when neither a browser nor a Grafana session is available.
.PP
The refresh loop exits cleanly on Ctrl\-C; per\-tick fetch failures (network blips, server restart) are rendered into the board rather than aborting the loop.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-addr\fR=\fIADDR\fR [default: http://localhost:8080]
Base URL of the target TensorWasm server. Must use \fBhttp://\fR or \fBhttps://\fR and have a non\-empty host.
.TP
\fB\-\-interval\fR=\fIINTERVAL\fR [default: 2]
Refresh interval, in seconds. Must be at least 1.
.TP
\fB\-\-tenant\fR=\fITENANT\fR [default: 0]
Tenant id to advertise on outbound API requests.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBTENSOR_WASM_TOKEN\fR
Bearer token attached as \fBAuthorization: Bearer ...\fR on each /healthz and /metrics fetch when set.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
TENSOR_WASM_TOKEN=devtoken tensor\-wasm observe \-\-addr https://tensor\-wasm.example.com \-\-interval 5
.fi
.RE
.SH NOTES
Cells render as \fB?\fR (for counts) or \fBn/a\fR (for percentages, latencies) when the underlying Prometheus series is absent from the scrape. The dashboard never substitutes a misleading zero.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
tensor\-wasm(1), tensor\-wasm\-metrics(1)
